!The Lojban Online Community

The lojban community has a vibrant and growing online presence. Only a portion of lojban websites
are listed here, as this community is growing and changing too fast to list them all.

Please also take a look at the ((Lojbanic Forums)) page, as the various lojbanic forums are an important part of the lojban community.

!!Lojbanic Websites
None of these sites are officially associated with the LLG in any way.
* [http://nehwon.dyn.wiw.org/jbovlaste/|jbovlaste] is an under-construction lojbanic dictionary program from [http://miranda.org/~jkominek/|Jay Kominek].
* [http://wiki.lojban.org/|The lojban Wiki] is a site that you can add to, hence participating directly in the non-LLG lojban community.    
*  The [http://selgre.lojban.org/|Lojban Portal] is an all-lojban page of lojban information, intended to supplant the main website for fluent speakers.
* [http://nuzban.wiw.org/|nuzban] is a news site entirely in lojban!
* [http://members.tripod.co.uk/lojbanlinks/|Lojban Links Page].
* ((Official LLG Projects|The official LLG Projects page))
* [http://www.tlg.uci.edu/~opoudjis/nick-loj.html|le la nitcion. sezyskinoi] - personal home page of [http://wiki.lojban.org/index.php?Nick%20Nicholas|Nick Nicholas]
* [http://www.epita.fr/~poss_r/lojban/|lojbo skicu] is elron's site.
* [http://www.nvg.org/~arj/dantimanti/|la danti manti] is [http://wiki.lojban.org/index.php?tsali|tsali's] very infrequently updated weblog
* [http://satirist.org/lojban/cuvjbo/balfihe/|la roldei balfipmabru] is [http://wiki.lojban.org/index.php?jezrax|jezrax's] site.
* [http://www.balvi.org/|balvi] is [http://wiki.lojban.org/index.php?xod|xod's] all-lojban webzine that explores political, cultural, and technological evolution from a positive (dynamist, extropian, third-wave) viewpoint
    
!!Lojbanic People
There are various people who are directly mentioned in official LLG documents and elsewhere on this site.  Some of them are listed here.  In particular, the current board and anyone working directly on this site are listed below; all the other criteria I thought of were either amazingly unwieldy or lended themselves to favoritism.

This is not intended, by any stretch, to be a listing of all the people involved in the lojban community.  For that, you probably want to look at [http://wiki.lojban.org/index.php?Info%20about%20individuals%20%28mostly%20lojbanists%29|the people page on the lojban wiki].  Most of the links below are to parts of the lojban Wiki.  The lojban Wiki is not an official LLG site.

As a general note, here are some of the places known to have a high concentration of Lojbanists, or some influential Lojbanists:
* Fairfax, Virginia
* New York, New York
* California
* Texas
* Israel
* Australia
* [http://www.lojban.org/resources/mailto:lojbab@lojban.org|Bob LeChevalier] is a founder of the LLG. This language might not exist without him and the others he worked with to make lojban public domain.  His lojbanic name is lojbab.
* [http://wiki.lojban.org/index.php?Nora%20LeChevalier|Nora LeChevalier] is lojbab's wife, and has done huge amounts of work on lojban, largely on the wordlists and software.
* [http://wiki.lojban.org/index.php?Nick%20Nicholas|Nick Nicholas] was the first fluent lojban speaker.  Well, he insists that he was the second, but he's known to be excessively modest.  He also has done a lot of lojbanic writing, both writing in lojban and about it.
* [http://wiki.lojban.org/index.php?John%20Cowan|John Cowan] is the author of the Complete Lojban Language. What more can you say?
* Shawn Lasseter is a local friend on the Le Chevalier's, on the	board, and does not currently have 'net access.
* [http://wiki.lojban.org/index.php?xod|xod] is on the board and very active in the community.
* [http://miranda.org/~jkominek/|Jay Kominek] is very active in the community and helps with this website.
* [http://www.lojban.org/resources/mailto:daltonG@digitalkingdom.org|Dalton Graham] is a friend of the webmaster and helps with this website.
* [http://www.digitalkingdom.org/~rlpowell/|Robin Lee Powell], yours truly, is the current webmaster of this site and the provider of the machine and bandwidth it is served from.
